<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zainal Abidin Syah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zainal Abidin Syah was sultan of Tidore in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a> from 1947 until his death in 1967. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a> he backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s claim to Dutch-held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-new-guinea">West New Guinea</a>, which Tidore had historically claimed as a dependency, and in 1956 he became the first governor of the Indonesian province of West Irian, with its seat at Soasio on Tidore. The sultanate then lapsed until its revival in 1999.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zainal-abidin-syah.jpg" alt="Zainal Abidin Syah" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author, published by Office of Library and Archives of Tidore City · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zainal_Abidin_Syah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
